   "text": "I read the structure as a symmetric dimer built around a hexa-aza cage, with a cyclic RGD-type peptide at each end. I did not run the SMILES through a parser, so validity is checked by hand only.\n\n**Cyclic peptide (each end).** The ring is cyclo(Asp\u2013Phe\u2013Lys\u2013Arg\u2013Gly), closed through backbone amides. The Lys side chain (four CH2) is acylated by a 3-maleimidopropanoyl group. That maleimide is attached to the thiol of a Cys-NH2 as a thiosuccinimide.\n\n**Linker to the cage (each end).**\n- The Cys \u03b1-NH is acylated by a 6-aminohexanoyl unit, and its amine nitrogen is acylated by the Tyr carbonyl.\n- The Tyr \u03b1-NH is acylated by a glutaryl group.\n- The other end of the glutaryl group forms an amide with the NH on a cage bridgehead carbon.\n\n**Cage.** Two bridgehead carbons, each bearing an NH amide. They are joined by three CH2\u2013NH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH\u2013CH2 bridges.\n\n**Stereochemistry.** I assumed L-Arg, L-Asp, L-Tyr and L-Cys, and D-Phe, as in the usual cyclo(RGDfK) peptide. I did not verify these against the individual wedges in the drawing. The Lys \u03b1-carbon is drawn with plain bonds, so I left it unspecified, as I did for the thiosuccinimide carbons.\n\nSMILES: O=C1CNC(=O)[C@H](CCCNC(N)=N)NC(=O)C(CCCCNC(=O)CCN2C(=O)CC(SC[C@@H](C(N)=O)NC(=O)CCCCCNC(=O)[C@H](Cc3ccc(O)cc3)NC(=O)CCCC(=O)NC45CNCCNCC(NC(=O)CCCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc6ccc(O)cc6)C(=O)NCCCCCC(=O)N[C@@H](CSC7CC(=O)N(C7=O)CCC(=O)NCCCCC8NC(=O)[C@@H](Cc9ccccc9)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(=O)O)NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@H](CCCNC(N)=N)NC8=O)C(N)=O)(CNCCNC4)CNCCNC5)C2=O)NC(=O)[C@@H](Cc%10ccccc%10)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(=O)O)N1"
